<title>USA: U.S. DEBT FUTURES END STEADY TO UP IN THIN TRADE.</title>
<headline>U.S. DEBT FUTURES END STEADY TO UP IN THIN TRADE.</headline>
<text>
<p>Aug 11 - U.S. debt futures ended steady to higher in thin trading after recovering late. Bounce tied to newswire interview with Fed's Phillips, who says no need for higher rates. Traders await retail sales, PPI and CPI later this week, say market prone to jitters until then.</p>
<p>((Chicago Derivatives Desk(312)408-8750))</p>
